                        <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_823">Caldbeck,
                                Cumberland. Parish church of St Kentigern</orgName><p>Fol. 220:
                                    <q>Orate pro bono salubri statu domini <persName
                                        key="person_3956">roberti Cooke</persName> et pro anima
                                    illius cum ab hac luce migraverit ac etiam pro animabus parentum
                                    suorum fratrum sororum et benefactorum qui dedit ecclesie
                                    paroch' de Cawlbeck istud missale. Calicem argentum Paxillum
                                    argent' duo pallia unum pallium lineum et superpellicum. Anno
                                    domini MDᵒVIᵒ.</q> Added mass for St Kentigern, the patron saint
                                of Caldbeck. See <bibl>Thomas Lees, <ref
                                        target="https://doi.org/10.5284/1064503">'S. Kentigern and
                                        his Dedications in Cumberland'</ref>, <title>Transactions of
                                        the Cumberland and Westmoreland Antiquarian and
                                        Archaeological Society</title> VI (1883), 333</bibl>, and
                                    <bibl>Dom Justin McCann, <ref
                                        target="http://www.ampleforthjournal.org/V_024.pdf">'A Sarum
                                        Missal'</ref>, <title>Ampleforth Journal</title> XXIV
                                    (1918), p. 4 (facsims).</bibl></p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners">Location recorded in MLGB2 as St Mary's
                            Catholic Church, Warwick Bridge, Carlisle (on deposit at Ampleforth
                            Abbey). The manuscript was returned to Carlisle in 2021; see <title><ref
                                    target="https://www.diocese.cc/FileSystem/11/Public/Publications/20/1491/pages.pdf"
                                    >The Catholic Voice</ref></title>, issue 334 (November
                            2021).</provenance>
